          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Quadrilaterals"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.449,
            0.971,
            0.551,
            0.984
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Reprint 2026-27"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.088,
            0.848,
            0.162
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "All these quadrilaterals are rectangles, including (iv). Quadrilateral (iv) is a rectangle because all its angles are 90°. However, it is a special kind of rectangle with all sides of equal length. We know that this quadrilateral is also called a square."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.162,
            0.847,
            0.199
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Square:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " A square is a quadrilateral in which all the angles are equal to 90°, and all the sides are of equal length."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.199,
            0.848,
            0.237
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Thus, every square is also a rectangle, but clearly every rectangle is not a square."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.278,
            0.253,
            0.714,
            0.433
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 5,
              "bbox": [
                0.278,
                0.253,
                0.714,
                0.433
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_9_image_5.jpg",
              "content": ""
            },
            {
              "type": "image_footnote",
              "index": 6,
              "bbox": [
                0.508,
                0.26,
                0.694,
                0.328
              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Wait, which one of them are you — an Indian or a Malayali? How can you be both?"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.446,
            0.848,
            0.519
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "This relation can be pictorially represented using a "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Venn diagram",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ". We have seen these diagrams before. In a Venn diagram, a set of objects is represented as points inside a closed curve. Typically, these closed curves are ovals or circles."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.52,
            0.681,
            0.539
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "For example, the set of all squares is represented as"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.311,
            0.57,
            0.378,
            0.619
          ],
